**What stands out:**
- **Studios:** Polyphony Digital has three games in the top 10 (GT7, Gran Turismo Sport and Gran Turismo 5), together about $2.35M. Insomniac (two Spider-Man games, ~$2.33M) and Santa Monica Studio (two God of War games, ~$2.28M) are close behind.
- **Recent games:** Spider-Man 2 ($954K), God of War Ragnarök ($900K) and Helldivers 2 ($700K) are newer and still earning, so they could move up the list.
- **Gross vs. net:** For most games, gross and net developer revenue are almost the same. Helldivers 2 has the biggest gap, about $40K (6%).

**How "lifetime" is measured:** I used gross digital revenue, which covers base games, DLC and in-game purchases. Hardware and subscription revenue aren't tied to individual games, so they're left out. "Lifetime" only covers the dates in the data. For most games that's about the first 4 years after release (for example, Horizon Zero Dawn runs from February 2017 to January 2021). Revenue after those dates isn't included.

