finance.text:
Our lifetime digital game revenue across all Sony titles is about **$19.2M gross**. Four franchises bring in more than half of it (57%):

- **God of War**: $3.43M (17.8%, 7 titles). God of War (2018) earned $1.38M of that and Ragnarök $0.90M.
- **Marvel's Spider-Man**: $2.99M (15.6%, 3 titles). Marvel's Spider-Man earned $1.38M, Spider-Man 2 $0.95M and Miles Morales $0.66M.
- **Gran Turismo**: $2.65M (13.8%, 4 titles). GT7 is the biggest at $0.90M.
- **Horizon**: $2.14M (11.1%, 5 titles). Horizon Zero Dawn earned $1.46M, the most of any single title.

The next tier is **MLB The Show** ($1.20M across 10 yearly releases), **The Last of Us** ($1.10M), **Ghost of Tsushima/Yōtei** ($0.98M) and **Helldivers 2** ($0.70M). Net revenue is almost the same as gross for nearly every franchise. The biggest gaps are Helldivers 2 (about 6% lower) and MLB The Show (about 3% lower).


