How these numbers were built:
- **Franchise grouping:** The data has no franchise field, so I grouped titles by name. For example, every "God of War" title, GT7 together with the Gran Turismo titles, and Uncharted counted apart from The Last of Us. Standalone games count as their own franchise.
- **What's included:** This is digital game revenue only (base games, DLC and microtransactions). Hardware and subscriptions can't be tied to a franchise, so they're left out.

analyst.text:
Our lifetime digital game revenue totals **$19.23M gross across 87 titles**, and it comes from 51 franchises. Three franchises bring in almost half of it:

- **God of War:** $3.43M from 7 titles (17.8%)
- **Marvel's Spider-Man:** $2.99M from 3 titles (15.6%)
- **Gran Turismo:** $2.65M from 4 titles (13.8%)

Next come **Horizon** ($2.14M, 11.1%), **MLB The Show** ($1.20M, but spread across 10 annual releases) and **The Last of Us** ($1.10M). After the top 10, revenue drops off fast. Most franchises in the bottom half made under $50K each.


