**What this covers and how it was matched:**
- **Digital game sales only.** That means base games, DLC and in-game purchases, at gross revenue. Hardware and subscriptions are left out because they aren't tied to specific games.
- **Where franchise comes from.** The sales data has no franchise field, so I took it from the game catalog, matching each title to its catalog game ID. The join was checked so totals aren't double-counted.
- **Titles matched by name.** 14 titles had no catalog ID, including The Last of Us Part II ($600K), God of War: Ascension and MLB The Show 17/22. I matched those by exact title name instead.
- **One title is unmatched.** **Ghost of Yōtei ($198K)** isn't in the catalog at all, so it's listed as "Unmapped." It would most likely belong to the Ghost of Tsushima franchise, which would raise that total to about $978K.

