Per correction: GAMES.FRANCHISE_NAME via distinct xref; unmapped labeled.
Our total lifetime game revenue is about **$19.23M** from 87 titles, spread over 51 franchises plus one "Unmapped" group.

**Key takeaways**
- **The top 3 franchises bring in almost half (47%) of revenue.** God of War has $3.43M (17.8%, 7 titles), Marvel's Spider-Man $2.99M (15.6%, 3 titles) and Gran Turismo $2.65M (13.8%, 4 titles).
- **Adding Horizon makes the top 4 worth $11.2M, or 58%.** Horizon has $2.14M (11.1%, 5 titles).
- **Marvel's Spider-Man earns the most per title, about $1.0M each.** God of War averages about $490K per title.
- **MLB The Show has the most titles (10) but earns only about $120K per title**, for $1.20M in total.
- **Single-title franchises can still earn a lot.** Ghost of Tsushima has $780K, Helldivers $700K and Bloodborne $420K. Bloodborne is in the Growth tier and is the first choice for any move into new genres.
- **The long tail is small.** About 30 franchises each have less than $50K, and together they make up under 3% of revenue.


