**How this was measured:**
- **What's counted:** Only digital game sales from the beginning of the data. Hardware and subscription revenue can't be tied to a game, so they're left out. Each title's revenue comes from the products it sells.
- **How titles were matched to engines:** I used each title's catalog game ID to find its engine in the game catalog. Each game has exactly one engine listed, so no revenue was counted twice.
- **What's missing:** 23 titles, worth $2.16M (11.2% of revenue), have no engine on record. If they were assigned engines, the order could change, though the gap between 4th and 5th place is about $1.5M.

